course: dictionary
lesson: 13865
title: Justify: giving good reasons
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: To justify something means to give a good reason for it, or to show that it is right or fair. Sometimes a reason is needed because someone has done or said something that might seem wrong. «Nothing justifies hitting.» The sentence says there is no good reason that could make hitting right.
explain: In maths and science, «Justify your answer» means do not just write the answer. Show why it is correct, using facts, numbers or working. Ravi wrote 12 and then showed 4 x 3 = 12 to justify it. His working is his proof.
explain: In stories and debates, characters justify their actions: they explain why they did something. «Mia justified being late by saying her bus had broken down.» Clue words such as because, since and so often show that a reason is coming.
explain: To check the meaning in a sentence, swap in «explain why it is right» and see if it still makes sense. If it does, you have found the meaning of justify.
fact: To justify something means to give a good reason for it, or to show that it is right or fair.
fact: «Justify your answer» means explain your reasoning with facts, numbers or working.
fact: When something justifies an action, it is a good reason for it, as in «Nothing justifies hitting».
fact: In computing, to justify text means to line it up so both edges are straight.
fact: The phrase «the ends justify the means» means some people think a good result can excuse a bad way of getting it.
exercise: Ravi says the answer is 12. What does «Justify your answer» ask him to do? | Ask a friend to tell him the answer | Show his working or reasons why 12 is correct | Write the answer again, but bigger | *Guess a different number
exercise: «Nothing justifies hitting.» What does justifies mean here? | Stops hitting from ever happening | Tells you it is fine to hit back | Makes hitting fun to do | *Means there is no good reason that could make hitting right
exercise: «Mia justified being late by saying her bus had broken down.» What did Mia do? | Said sorry and never came late again | *Gave a reason for being late | Blamed her brother for the delay | Ran to school very fast
test: Which phrase means you must explain why your answer is right? | Show your teeth | *Justify your answer | Draw a straight line | Count the stars
test: «The captain tried to justify his choice to the crew.» What did the captain try to do? | Hide his choice from everyone | Change his choice without telling anyone | Forget his choice | *Explain why his choice was right
exam: Which sentence uses justify correctly to mean give a good reason? | I justified my lunch by eating it quickly | The teacher asked me to justify my late homework, so I told her about the flood | The dog justified the ball across the park | *The sea was justified by the big waves
